      "content": "Thanks for that. It's a good start, but I'm a bit worried it still feels a little... \"polite\"? Like, it covers all the bases, but it might be a bit too safe for Oxford. \n\nI just got an email from a colleague who's been through this before. They mentioned that the keyword filter is actually quite sensitive—like, if it doesn't see a high density of those specific \"high-impact\" terms, the score drops significantly and the profile doesn't even make it to the human reviewers. \n\nThe paragraph you wrote is decent, but I'm nervous it's too \"light\" on the terminology to actually pass the automated stage. Can you try expanding this into a full opening section—maybe 2-3 paragraphs? Try to weave those concepts in more deeply so they feel central to the actual argument, but I'm telling you again: please don't just pile them in for the sake of it. If it sounds like a word salad, I'm doomed. I need it to be dense with those specific terms so the filter is happy, but the actual writing still needs to be sophisticated and scholarly.",
